<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    SystemUI's own copy of the corner geometry for arcfox (Razr 50 Ultra).

    SystemUI does NOT reuse the framework's rounded_corner_radius. It keeps its
    own pair:

      real_rounded_corner_radius     the radius it uses to draw the corner
                                     overlay and to decide how far to inset
                                     status-bar content
      rounded_corner_content_padding the horizontal padding applied to the status
                                     bar so text and icons clear the curve

    With both left at the AOSP defaults, the framework-side fix in
    core/res/.../config.xml is not enough on its own: the corners get reported
    correctly but SystemUI still lays the clock out as if the panel were square.
    That is why both files change together.

    Values read with aapt2 from Motorola's own overlay in the W1UXS36H dump,
    product/overlay/SystemUI__arcfox_g__auto_generated_rro_product.apk:

        dimen/real_rounded_corner_radius        103px
        dimen/rounded_corner_content_padding     27px

    Note 103px here against 100px for the framework's rounded_corner_radius.
    That 3px difference is Motorola's, not a transcription slip. SystemUI
    deliberately draws its anti-aliased corner overlay very slightly proud of the
    layout radius so no lit pixel survives at the edge of the curve. Do not
    "correct" them to match.

    Deliberately NOT copied from the same overlay yet, because each needs its own
    verification and none of them is the reported bug:
      * config_enableDisplayCutoutProtection / config_frontBuiltInDisplayCutoutProtection
        (the camera-privacy ring drawn around the punch-hole)
      * cli_status_bar_height and the cli_* family, which belong to the cover
        display and are only meaningful once the cover panel is driven properly.
-->
<resources>
    <dimen name="real_rounded_corner_radius">103px</dimen>
    <dimen name="rounded_corner_content_padding">27px</dimen>
</resources>
